ss_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"y1KXhvxpNHEeSmBGe6fuHA","review_id":"ADH5h4wnsA48tdGLXiciog","date":"2014-08-06T14:17:59","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.934701681137085,"text_excerpt":"Stopped in for drinks with the work crew. The bar area was large enough for all of us and the drinks were very good. Bartender knew how to make an Old Fashioned properly and it was great. Had a good selection of beer and spirits. Another hit was the Cajun martini with pepper, olive and garlic infused vodka, hot sauce, olive juice, rimmed with creole seasonong and garnished with pickled green beans."},{"business_id":"y1KXhvxpNHEeSmBGe6fuHA","review_id":"l5SrOlj8jKjBApXudYtDSg","date":"2015-01-27T22:00:53","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9347016215324402,"text_excerpt":"I was thrilled with the Retouvailles Bistro. We chose this for lunch when looking for Creole food. This is another second floor restaurant on Bourbon Street where the food is served either in the bar or on a great balcony. The weather was cold - we started with a table overlooking Bourbon Street. It was too chilly, so we went inside instead. Let me start by saying that our server was wonderful. I wish I had gotten his name, but he was kind, friendly and very helpful. I had an Oyster Po-Boy. In my few days in New Orleans I think I had three Oyster Po-Boys and this one was the best. The Oysters were large, lightly breaded and fried. It was served on a roll with lettuce, tomato and pickles. ..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"y1KXhvxpNHEeSmBGe6fuHA","photo_id":"sDIL2RVdvIPq4_nyvZA5aw","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/sDIL2RVdvIPq4_nyvZA5aw.jpg","visual_representativeness":1.0000001192092896}]},"notebook_case":null}
